  "data": {
    "title": "Long-Term Effects of Attentional Performance on Functional Brain Network Topology",
    "text": "Title: Long-Term Effects of Attentional Performance on Functional Brain Network Topology\n\nFMRI Data Processing and Time-series Analysis\nThe functional images were spatially normalized to MNI space and regionally parcellated using a template image comprising 442 cortical and subcortical brain regions to estimate the mean fMRI time series for each region for each participant. The parcellation was based on the AAL template, which was sub-parcellated into 442 smaller regions.\n\nEach regional time series was band-pass filtered (wavelet scale 3: 0.042–0.083 Hz) using the maximum overlap discrete wavelet transform (MODWT). For each pair of nodes the wavelet correlation was estimated and the absolute correlation values resulted in a 442 × 442 association matrix.\n\nTopological Metrics of Brain Graphs\nBinary graphs of different connection densities were constructed based on the association matrix. A thresholding algorithm starting with the minimum spanning tree (MST) was used, followed by adding highest correlations iteratively. Graphs at 15 different cost levels were constructed in the range of 2.5%–50% connection density.\n\nBased on these adjacency matrices we calculated global efficiency, nodal efficiency, and local efficiency (clustering coefficient). Graph metrics were calculated for each cost level and averaged across the entire cost range to avoid dependence on a single threshold."
  },
